@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@
+# Native Gaudi2 resources
+
+`src/core/gaudi2/runtime.h` and `.cpp` provide the first native SynapseAI resource
+boundary for the future Qwen runner. They call the real C API directly: initialize
+and acquire Gaudi2, allocate device and pinned Host storage, create streams, queue
+H2D/D2H copies, record/query/wait events and query free/total memory. The resource
+layer also compiles native graphs into bounded-workspace recipes and owns compute
+completion. The closed [BF16 GEMM Op](gaudi2-bf16-gemm.md) owns the first graph's
+mathematics; this layer does not substitute a PyTorch inference worker.
+
+One standalone native session owns one Gaudi2 device. Resource objects retain
+that session, so releasing the `Device` facade before a pending transfer does not
+release the physical device. Device facades may be copied but cannot be moved.
+The runner serializes calls to these objects; this is not a concurrent allocator.
+The owner must not coexist with an independently initialized SynapseAI/PyTorch
+session in the same process.
+
+An upload/download obtains exclusive leases on both operands until its event
+completes. `PinnedBuffer::bytes()`, `DeviceBuffer::address()` and another transfer
+reject an outstanding lease. Previously returned spans/addresses must not be used
+while leased. Each `Transfer` retains its stream and both allocations. `wait()`
+and successful `ready()` release the leases; destroying a pending transfer waits.
+Moving over a pending transfer first completes the old one. A failed copy submit
+or event record drains the stream before releasing either operand, including an
+ambiguous submit that may have enqueued some work before returning an error.
+
+Explicit wait/query errors throw `SynapseError` with the actual `synStatus` and
+keep the leases. A caller may retry a recoverable wait. Destruction cannot silently
+free possibly active DMA buffers: an unsuccessful final fence or native cleanup
+terminates the process. Callers should explicitly wait while they can handle and
+report an error. Range checks reject zero-length/out-of-allocation copies before
+submission. Buffer allocation sizes are explicit; model/Host budget policy remains
+the runner's responsibility.
+
+`Stream::native_handle()` permits future recipe integration. External queued
+compute must retain its own buffers and completion fences. A `Transfer` retains
+only the operands of its own copy. The native GEMM's separate `Compute` owns its
+recipe, workspace and all device operands. There is no `synStreamWaitEvent`/cross-stream
+compute dependency implementation in this increment and no claim of compute/DMA
+overlap, recipe completion ownership or asynchronous model inference.
+
+## Build and offline qualification
+
+The existing `NINFER_GAUDI2_PREPARATION_ONLY=ON` build includes
+`ninfer-gaudi2-runtime-lifecycle-test`. It compiles the production adapter source
+against a private, test-only C API double. The fake queues copies and only applies
+them on a fence/stream drain. Freeing a still-referenced operand or releasing a
+device with live resources fails the test. It also deliberately queues a copy
+before an injected submit error to verify the failure cleanup path.
+
+The fake header is guarded by `NINFER_GAUDI2_RUNTIME_TEST_FAKE`, defined only for
+that test target. It is never linked into the product adapter or selected as a
+fallback when the real SDK is missing. Offline tests establish Host ownership,
+ordering and failure behavior; they do not establish DMA/driver correctness.
+
+For an explicit compile-only check against an actual SDK:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S backends/ninfer -B build-gaudi2-sdk -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DNINFER_GAUDI2_SDK_HEADER_CHECK=ON \
+  -DNINFER_SYNAPSE_INCLUDE_DIR=/path/to/sdk/include/habanalabs
+cmake --build build-gaudi2-sdk --config Release --target ninfer_gaudi2_runtime_sdk_check -j
+```
+
+On MSVC this object target explicitly uses `/utf-8 /EHsc`: official UTF-8 SDK
+comments must not be decoded using the Windows system code page, and exception
+unwinding is required for resource cleanup. The vendor SDK include directory is
+`SYSTEM`; project source remains subject to the caller's warning policy. This
+target was also built through CMake with `CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="/W4 /WX"` on CP936
+Windows. These options are scoped to the SDK object target and do not change the
+existing CUDA Engine targets.
+
+For the native Linux library and an explicitly invoked 4096-byte DMA round trip:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S backends/ninfer -B build-gaudi2-native -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DNINFER_GAUDI2_NATIVE_RUNTIME=ON \
+  -DNINFER_SYNAPSE_INCLUDE_DIR=/usr/include/habanalabs \
+  -DNINFER_SYNAPSE_LIBRARY=/path/to/libSynapse.so
+cmake --build build-gaudi2-native --config Release -j
+build-gaudi2-native/src/core/gaudi2/ninfer-gaudi2-dma-smoke
+```
+
+Native configuration requires Linux, actual headers and `libSynapse`. Missing
+SDK components fail configuration. The hardware smoke is not registered as a
+host-only CTest and is never run automatically in an environment without Gaudi2.
+These instructions apply from the wrapper root after preparing the backend;
+use `-S .` from a standalone prepared NInfer tree.
+
+## Evidence and remaining work
+
+The adapter was independently compiled, without linking or initialization, against
+official SynapseAI **1.24.1-482** headers using MSVC 14.44 x64, C++20, `/W4 /WX`
+(vendor headers excluded from project warnings). All 163 extracted SDK headers
+were checked against the verified extraction manifest. The original package was
+verified after writing using SHA256
+`66b7f816a9c2fa5ae125c5ab0c1f104dc555c58026bdc5f43b2f673fa4484e1b`.
+The package was obtained from the
+[official package repository](https://vault.habana.ai/artifactory/debian/jammy/pool/main/h/habanalabs-graph/habanalabs-graph_1.24.1-482_amd64.deb),
+following the [official installation package description](https://docs.habana.ai/en/latest/Installation_Guide/Custom_Driver_and_Software_Installation.html).
+SDK files are local build prerequisites and are not copied into this repository.
+
+The production call patterns were checked against the official PyTorch bridge
+[stream implementation](https://github.com/HabanaAI/gaudi-pytorch-bridge/blob/5176b1b2d6865608514e83a2b1fd66459920676e/backend/synapse_helpers/stream.cpp)
+and its device/Host-memory/event helpers. SynapseAI_Core's no-op stream/event
+demonstrations are not used as an execution implementation.
+
+The offline tests cover deferred round trips and offsets, event scope, duplicate
+session rejection, operand reuse, move assignment, facade destruction order,
+empty/range failures, failed allocation/create/submit/record/query/wait and retry.
+Linux linking, driver initialization, physical DMA, SDK failure semantics, actual
+HBM/free-memory observations and the smoke executable remain unverified without
+a Gaudi2 environment. Native static GEMM recipe construction/launch ownership is
+implemented and offline tested; physical MME execution, TPC dequantization,
+GDN/full-KV, model generation and KVMem device integration remain to be qualified
+or implemented. No throughput or HPU memory-peak claim is made.
